 ## Overview
-This method defines the data layout and generation process for creating GPU-ready instance data for blocky voxel meshes. It solves the problem of efficiently packing per-face texture IDs and color tints into a contiguous structure that can be submitted to the graphics API. It differs from sibling methods by focusing on the specific `BlockRenderData` struct layout and the logic for mixing or replacing base block tints with face-specific tints before instance submission.
+This method defines the data structure and generation logic for translating discrete voxel face attributes into GPU-drawable instances. It solves the problem of mapping per-face texture IDs and color tints to a unified instance buffer for efficient rendering. It differs from sibling methods by focusing on the specific aggregation of face-level metadata (textures and tints) into a single struct per block, rather than the broader mesh assembly or plugin architecture.
 
